// APW-2 — Approval replay (approval never consumed) — BUGGY variant.
//
// SOURCE (verbatim, practitioner-written):
//   Classmethod, "AgentCore Gateway Dogwood temporal policies", 2026-09-14.
//   https://dev.classmethod.jp/articles/agentcore-gateway-dogwood-temporal-policies/
//   policy: gateway/OrderAfterCartCheck.dw
//
// Stated intent (from the tutorial): "order only after the cart has been
// confirmed" — allow place_order only if a get_cart RESPONSE with the SAME
// cartId / store / amount was seen within the last minute.
//
// The weakness (APW-2): nothing *consumes* that cart-check. One
// get_cart::response therefore authorises EVERY matching place_order in the
// window. A parallel burst of N orders, all matching that single cart-check,
// are all admitted — one verification authorises N actions.
//
// Framing (pattern education, NOT a vulnerability disclosure):
//   "If your intent is one approval -> one action, this policy does not
//    enforce it."
//
// Namespace: AgentCore (as authored in the public tutorial). Phase 1 will
// normalize to the repo's Drupe namespace for the ROTN parser.
@id("apw2_order_after_cart_check_buggy")
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___place_order",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
when {
    context.input.amount > 0 && context.input.amount <= 3000
}
when temporal {
    formerly within 1m AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___get_cart"::response {
        eventResource: resource,
        output.cartId: context.input.cartId,
        output.store: context.input.store,
        output.amount: context.input.amount
    }
};
